{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וזבחת פסח", :translit "v'zavachta pesach", :gloss "and you shall slaughter the Paschal offering"} {:he "לא תאכל עליו חמץ", :translit "lo tokhal alav chametz", :gloss "you shall not eat leavened bread upon it"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Semikhut ha-ketav: inference drawn from the verbal phrase 'upon it (עליו)' in the adjacent verse referring back to the Paschal offering, taken to mean 'on account of it.'"}], :frame {:text "The phrase לא תאכל עליו חמץ (Deuteronomy 16:3) is read as prohibiting slaughter of the Paschal lamb while leaven is still in one's possession. The word עליו is understood midrashically as 'on account of it' — one must not slaughter the offering while chametz remains. This reading is reflected in the halakhic principle that removal of chametz precedes the Paschal slaughter, as codified in Pesachim 5a and Mechilta de-Rabbi Yishmael, Bo, Massechta de-Pischa 5.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 16:3" "Pesachim 5a" "Mechilta de-Rabbi Yishmael, Bo, Massechta de-Pischa 5"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Semikhut ha-ketav: inference drawn from the verbal phrase 'upon it (עליו)' in the adjacent verse referring back to the Paschal offering, taken to mean 'on account of it.'", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:36:51.359311803Z", :model "glm-5.2"}